Conclusion: User setting sources gate user memory, not the Project/Local walk through ancestor folders. claudeMdExcludes filters all three types, including rules. Managed/policy memory cannot be excluded. No model session was started for this inspection.

Public docs corroboration, fetched 2026-10-31 from https://code.claude.com/docs/en/memory.md:
- "CLAUDE.md and CLAUDE.local.md files in the directory hierarchy above the working directory are loaded at launch."
- "The claudeMdExcludes setting lets you skip specific files by path or glob pattern."
- "Patterns are matched against absolute file paths using glob syntax."
- "You can configure claudeMdExcludes at any settings layer: user, project, local, or managed policy. Arrays merge across layers."
- The example excludes a parent rules directory with /home/user/monorepo/other-team/.claude/rules/**.
- Either the discovered path or the symlink target may match an exclusion since v2.1.239.

Help check: claude --version reported 2.1.310. claude --help lists --settings, --setting-sources and --strict-mcp-config. --bare disables CLAUDE.md discovery and OAuth/keychain reads, so it is not the selected solution. --safe-mode also removes the tree's instructions, so it is not selected. The existing claude-help.log records this installed help surface.
